    </packagedElement>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193196_48088_23771" xmi:uuid="170c9537-be75-4672-a016-dbda23164b7e" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455721030337_630909_43088" xmi:uuid="2d97e359-b13d-4444-b33d-6055d7e0060b" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193196_48088_23771"/>
        <body>A ProductConfiguration is a manufacturable object or expected as so. A ProductConfiguration is defined with respect to the ProductClass it is a member of. &lt;note&gt; The kind of product that is to be manufactured from the data of the ProductConfiguration, is the kind of product that the MemberOf identifies a class of. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; The intent of ProductConfiguration is the identification of one manufacturable object whereas the intent of ProductClass is the gathering of products with similar characteristics. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt; A ProductConfiguration that is associated with a ProductClass that identifies a family of diesel engines is intended to lead to the manufacture of a specific case of diesel engine, and the ProductConfiguration that is associated with a ProductClass that identifies a car family will lead to the manufacture of a car. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;note&gt; The entity ProductConfiguration corresponds to the concept of configuration item defined, in some configuration management standards, as an item subject to configuration management. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt; A ProductConfiguration may represent a component of a contracted product, onto which severe safety rules apply and for which configuration management is therefore rigorously applied. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;note&gt; A ProductConfiguration may identify a variation of a ProductClass, an entire ProductClass, or some portion thereof. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; A ProductConfiguration can be established prior to the existence of a corresponding product.&lt;/note&gt; For a ProductConfiguration one or more additional Specification objects may be specified. In this case they enhance the characterization provided for the associated ProductClass. &lt;note&gt; The actual set of Specification objects for a ProductConfiguration are obtained by the union of DefiningSpecifications and of the Specification objects related to the &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_ProductSpecificationAndConfiguration.htm#SpecificationAssignment.AssignedTo&lt;/path&gt; AssignedTo&lt;/a&gt; through a SpecificationAssignment or a SpecificationConditionAssignment with AssociationType 'identification' or 'non-replaceable standard'. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; The specification of a ProductConfiguration may be incomplete: there may not be in DefiningSpecifications any instance of Specification for some SpecificationCategory declared as mandatory for the &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_ProductSpecificationAndConfiguration.htm#SpecificationAssignment.AssignedTo&lt;/path&gt; AssignedTo&lt;/a&gt;. For these SpecificationCategory objects any Specification available in the context of the &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_ProductSpecificationAndConfiguration.htm#SpecificationAssignment.AssignedTo&lt;/path&gt; AssignedTo&lt;/a&gt; is considered as valid for the manufacturing of the product characterized by the considered SpecificationAssignment. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt; If the colour is not specified for a given car family, the vehicle resulting from the realization of a ProductConfiguration associated to the ProductClass representing the car family may be without paint or painted in any available colour. &lt;/example&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551199927346_720838_127786" xmi:uuid="b44d7d3c-735c-4680-a473-487cb2a68c9a" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_290014c_1550847743191_208266_98071"/>
        <body>These flowports are not bound to the ARM target because only a product definition property type can be assigned to it.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>ProductConfiguration</name>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193950_639198_28422" xmi:uuid="0ba60033-a7b2-4fa1-8190-d33c865b9f12" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
