      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194073_190549_28981" xmi:uuid="940ba4f7-c098-4b65-be44-6520f7573095" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455723825787_217248_43136" xmi:uuid="c26a6a4c-22c5-42db-9da0-4d65184f0db4" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194073_190549_28981"/>
          <body> specifies whether the Specification objects within the SpecificationCategory are mutually exclusive for the production of one specific product. A value of 'true' indicates that the referenced objects are mutually exclusive for the production of the specific product. &lt;example&gt; 'safety equipment' is an example for a non-mutually exclusive SpecificationCategory if ABS and air bag are Specification objects in this category. 'engine' is an example for a SpecificationCategory with an implicitExclusiveCondition since usually only one engine can be mounted for power supply. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;note&gt; More complex conditions can be handled using Condition objects.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
        </ownedComment>
