      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193944_142474_28391" xmi:uuid="d623ee06-cdd5-4dc8-a3ea-3d2c88ee7758" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455720430517_882259_43066" xmi:uuid="f9fbdd47-5b9b-4db9-966e-98839bdfd0a5" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193944_142474_28391"/>
          <body> the identification or set of identifications of a specific version of the ProductClass. The value of this attribute need not be specified. &lt;note&gt; This attribute supports multi-identification in different contexts as described in Fundamental concepts and assumptions.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>VersionId</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193119_518292_23608"/>
        <lowerValue xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194704_37649_34080" xmi:uuid="fcdf0121-4ac8-4ede-a493-e82ee7c9eb78" xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger"/>
        <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
        <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193747_790380_27312"/>
      </ownedAttribute>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193944_697354_28392" xmi:uuid="d9a1fc3a-4340-42e9-840b-3167b1380f96" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455720456820_525685_43067" xmi:uuid="9eb67de2-fc3e-4c03-8f21-c79d61f9bd24" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193944_697354_28392"/>
          <body> the level of the ProductClass in a hierarchical structure of ProductClass objects. &lt;example&gt; A high level ProductClass (LevelType = 'enterprise') may be used to define all SpecificationCategory and Specification objects for all ProductClass objects of an enterprise with several brands and companies. A second level ProductClass (LevelType = 'platform') may be used to group all products that are based on the same technical concept (platform); these products may belong to different brands. A third level ProductClass (LevelType = 'car family') may be used to group all products that have a common base and a fixed set of characteristics (specification categories). A fourth level ProductClass (LevelType = 'car type') may represent products that are offered to the market; this level of ProductClass may be defined by the marketing department. A set of specifications sufficient to produce the car is associated with its ProductClass. Within this association, a distinction is made between standard characteristics (such as number of doors) and options that have to be chosen (such as outside colour) or that may be chosen by the customer (such as radio).&lt;/example&gt; The value of this attribute need not be specified. </body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>LevelType</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193042_855579_23449"/>
