    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193254_579461_23857" xmi:uuid="f85d51fc-b4ed-48bd-9077-df43a1099396" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455726057185_840765_43172" xmi:uuid="3c0de355-2f8f-4220-a634-e17f8342f28c" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193254_579461_23857"/>
        <body>A SpecificationInclusion is a representation of the statement that specifies that the application of a Specification or of a Condition implies the inclusion of an additional Specification or Condition. &lt;example&gt;The source of such a completion may be a customer order. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;note&gt; The SpecificationInclusion is intended to complete the set of Specification objects for a BreakdownVersionAssignment in order to enable the manufacturing of the product on the basis of an initial set of Specification objects defined. &lt;/note&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>SpecificationInclusion</name>
